   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Digital Economy Programme (PDEP) is a regional program led by the UN Capital Development Fund (UNCDF), funded by Australia, the EU and New Zealand supporting the development of inclusive digital economies in the Pacific. The PDEP has played a pivotal role facilitating financial inclusion, digitization and empowering customers. For example in Kiribati, PDEP facilitated a &#x2018;G2P Digital Payment Expansion project&#x2019; which piloted opening bank accounts for social welfare payment recipients. This pilot led to 79% of rural citizens opting-in for a bank account wallet disbursement over receiving physical cash, resulting in a dramatic lift in financial literacy, financial inclusion, convenience and reducing risks to personal safety. A follow-up survey conducted in June 2025 revealed that nearly 85% of beneficiaries in mainland Tarawa expressed willingness to switch to digital payment channels for their other banking needs. Following this, the Ministry of Women, Youth and Social Affairs (MWYSA), the Ministry of Finance and Economic Development (MFED) and ANZ Bank developed a workplan for scaling up the project to reach 30,000 citizens (a fifth of the population).</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
